---
description: Pull for lifecycle states, work-plan prerequisites, spec-then-tests-then-code, Tito decide-versus-ask, or config-layer order.
alwaysApply: false
---
States: `DISCOVERY`, `PLANNED`, `APPROVED`, `IMPLEMENTING`, `READY_FOR_REVIEW`, `APPROVED_FOR_COMMIT`, `DONE`. `PLANNED` has five plan sections. Skip the plan only on clear instruction. Implement only after approval.
Work-plan: independent read-only slices may be ready together. Do not silently pick a ready implementation slice. Review may start at `READY_FOR_REVIEW`. `client-careful` and independent review wait for `APPROVED_FOR_COMMIT`; `solo-balanced` and `solo-fast` ordinary dependents may proceed at `READY_FOR_REVIEW`.
Code: spec doc from Docs impact, then failing approved tests, then code. Waive the spec doc when nothing changes behavior.
Decides, then reports: naming, file placement, internal structure, test approach, stacking a branch on an approved dependency, accepting a writer's sensible deviation, sending a writer/finisher back to restore the approved spec or docs gate, small in-scope docs fixes, routing-table model choice, and one obvious reading of a request.
Asks, and stops, for product vision or scope, a new command or write behavior (Plan), a new dependency, a public CLI/API contract, a data or schema migration, security or permissions, premium-model fan-out, push, a PR when `git.autoPullRequest` is not true, a merge when `git.autoMerge` is not true, deploy, delete, `--confirm` cleanups, and the safety floor. Later updates carry one `Decided:` line.
Config order: core safety floor, project risk profile, domain packs, technology packs, project rules and docs, current task instructions. A task may increase caution, never silently weaken the safety floor.
